{"document": "Proliferation Financing National Risk Assessment (July 2026)", "term": "TFS", "definition": "Targeted Financial Sanctions means both asset freezing and prohibitions to prevent funds or other assets from being made available, directly or indirectly, to or for the benefit of UN designated persons and entities (including certain maritime vessels). For the purposes of this NRA, the TFS measures are contained in the UNSCRs relating to the prevention, suppression and disruption of proliferation of weapons of mass destruction and its financing (i.e. DPRK and Iran). These are more specifically described in Part II(b) of Annex C to the FATF Guidance on Proliferation Financing144. In addition to the asset freeze requirements and prohibitions on making funds and other economic resources available to, or for the benefit of, designated persons (including entities), these measures include - •requirement to close representative offices of designated entities •prohibiting designated entities from participating in joint ventures or any other business arrangement"}
{"document": "Proliferation Financing National Risk Assessment (July 2026)", "term": "Themis", "definition": "The FIU's online reporting mechanism, which is the single point of contact for supervised entities in relation to: Reporting under the Proceeds of Crime or Terrorism Legislation; Reporting under Section 24 of the FIU Act; Reporting Sanction Breaches. Themis is also the tool the FIU use for communicating advisory notices and other pieces of information."}
